 Reads vendor order exports (CSV), normalizes the columns, drops duplicate orders and posts the rows to the warehouse HTTP API at `WAREHOUSE_URL`.
 
-Supported vendors: `vendor_a`, `vendor_b`.
+Supported vendors: `vendor_a`, `vendor_b`, `vendor_c`.
+
+Vendor C exports use UTF-8 encoding. Its `orderNumber`, `productCode`,
+`totalPrice`, and `orderedAt` columns map to `order_id`, `sku`, `amount`, and
+`created_at`. ISO-8601 timestamps must include a UTC offset (or `Z`) and are
+converted to UTC using that offset. Invalid timestamps or missing offsets
+raise an error.
 
 Vendor B exports use Latin-1 encoding. Its `ref`, `article`, `montant`, and
 `date_commande` columns map to `order_id`, `sku`, `amount`, and `created_at`.
